    "text": "In the book ’Never Mind, We’ll Do It Ourselves’, the authors revealed the backstory in the secret development and initial deployment of the Predator drone, in 2000. While the Predator was not developed by a commercial enterprise, it still required a rogue group of inter-departmental individuals to drag it into existence and use its initial operations as a forceful example of potential against standing military othodoxy.\nEver since the U.S. Army court martialed Billy Mitchell for the crime of being absolutely correct about the future of airpower, the U.S. military has slowly gotten better at innovation. But it still has a long way to go to match the speed of commerce.",
